guide forever/reputation/thunder-bluff
title Thunder Bluff Reputation
category Reputation
folder Reputation · Cities
faction Horde
levels 12-60
zone Thunder Bluff
keywords Thunder Bluff, Rumstag Proudstrider, cloth quartermaster, cloth donation, Runecloth, Additional Runecloth, Wool, Silk, Mageweave, Morrowgrain, Evergreen Pouch, Bashana Runetotem, Storm Shadowhoof, Shy-Rotam, Guarding Secrets, Camp Narache, Bloodhoof Village, Gloomrise, kodo mount, Harb Clawhoof
reward text Exalted with Thunder Bluff
reward item 18793
why Winterspring's level 56-60 quests, Morrowgrain and Runecloth to Exalted, with Mulgore's old quests as an optional extra.

# Built from Forever's quest data: every quest that pays Thunder Bluff
# reputation, with the value from Forever's own quest pages, the world
# database (quest chains, the cloth quests' exclusive group,
# Additional Runecloth's repeat flag), quests.json, npcs.json, items.json and
# the quest notes for givers, objectives, drops and places, and the Forever
# client's Faction and ItemSparse tables.
# Numbers (Forever's quest pages): A Donation of Wool, Silk, Mageweave and
# Runecloth 150 each (60 cloth); Additional Runecloth 50 for 20 Runecloth (the
# same as Classic Era);
# Morrowgrain to Thunder Bluff 50 for 10 Morrowgrain, repeatable, quest level
# 55 (full at 60). In Forever's data Un'Goro Soil is handed to Ghede in
# Thunder Bluff and the Evergreen Pouch and Tharlendris Seeds are sold by
# Bashana Runetotem.
# Starting standing (Faction table): Tauren Friendly 1000; Orc, Troll and
# Skyborne Friendly 100; Undead Neutral 500. No race has a reputation bonus.
# The Legacy perk Diplomat adds 2% a rank, 10% at 5/5: the numbers here leave
# it out. City reputation also gives a quarter to the other Horde cities
# (Faction table: parent Horde, 0.25), except starting-zone quests.
# Low-level quests: in Classic a quest 6 or more levels below you pays less, a
# fifth at 60; quests of level 55 and up pay in full at 60, so the Winterspring
# chain comes first. The old hubs are optional steps (the first step of each
# carries a label; skipping it skips the hub), ranked by reputation per minute
# at full value with the fifth beside it.
# INGAME: grey-quest reputation at 60 (Classic: a fifth from 9 levels below; one Forever beta report: full, quest 456 at level 30 paid 100)
# INGAME: reputation discounts in Forever (Classic: 10% at Honored with the city's merchants; Forever guide sites report 5/10/15/20% from Friendly to Exalted, one says not announced)
# Morrowgrain: the world database's loot table for the Evergreen Herb Casing
# holds Morrowgrain 37% of the time, 1 to 5 of it (about 1.1 a casing).
# ASSUMED: the Evergreen Pouch can be used once every 10 minutes (Classic; Forever's data has no cooldown for it). In-game check: the pouch's cooldown after one use.
# Left out: class letters and the Tauren-only well chain (Poison Water to
# Wildmane Cleansing), race-only breadcrumbs, dungeon quests (Disharmony of
# Fire in Blackrock Depths, 150, named in a tip), Commendation Signets (only
# from the Ahn'Qiraj war effort), The Mark of Quality and Improved Quality
# (Feralas yeti hides, level 46-48) and Perfect Yeti Hide (a 3% drop).
# Mounts: the client lets every Horde race ride every Horde mount and puts no
# reputation gate on them.
# ASSUMED: another race's kodos need Exalted with Thunder Bluff (Classic rule; Forever's client puts no reputation gate on the items, so the vendor decides). In-game check: a non-tauren below Exalted at Harb Clawhoof.

step Thunder Bluff: how it works
  tip Thunder Bluff reputation comes from quests, Morrowgrain and cloth. Rumstag Proudstrider, the cloth quartermaster, stands on the central rise among the leatherworkers' and tailors' tents. He takes four one-time donations of 60 cloth (150 each) and then Additional Runecloth, 20 Runecloth for 50, as often as you like. Every point you earn with Thunder Bluff also gives a quarter as much to Orgrimmar, the Undercity and the Darkspear Trolls. While you level, do Thunder Bluff's quests within 5 levels of them: Mulgore at 1 to 12, Camp Taurajo and the Crossroads at 13 to 22, Thousand Needles at 25 to 30. The Legacy perk Diplomat adds up to 10%. Rewards: at Honored Thunder Bluff's merchants sell to you for 10% less (the Classic rule), the kodo vendor included; at Exalted other races can buy the kodos: 20 gold for a level 40 kodo, 200 gold for a great kodo at level 60, once you have mount training. Thunder Bluff has no tabard or other reward.
  accept 7820                         -- Rumstag Proudstrider: A Donation of Wool, +150

step Everlook: Storm Shadowhoof
  zone Winterspring
  tip Storm Shadowhoof's four quests are level 56 to 60, so they pay in full: 400 Thunder Bluff reputation. Ursius, an elite bear, walks a loop over the four hills north of Everlook: wait on a hilltop for him.
  level 55
  accept 5054                         -- Ursius of the Shardtooth, +100
  kill 10806 quest 5054.1             -- Ursius, elite
  turnin 5054
  accept 5055                         -- Brumeran of the Chillwind, +100

step Brumeran and Shy-Rotam
  tip Brumeran, an elite chimera, spawns south of Everlook. For Shy-Rotam, kill frostsabers north of Everlook until one drops Sacred Frostsaber Meat (about one in ten), then use the meat at the Stone of Shy-Rotam, far to the north, and kill the great cat that comes. If you have done Trull Failbane's Wild Guardians quests (the Orgrimmar guide), the Crazed, Moontouched and Berserk owlbeasts around Everlook sometimes drop a Blue-feathered Necklace: it starts Guarding Secrets, 50 Orgrimmar and then 100 Thunder Bluff reputation in full.
  kill 10807 quest 5055.1             -- Brumeran, elite
  turnin 5055                         -- Storm Shadowhoof
  accept 5056                         -- Shy-Rotam, +150
  collect 12733 optional              -- Sacred Frostsaber Meat, from the frostsabers
  kill 10737 quest 5056.1             -- Shy-Rotam
  turnin 5056                         -- Storm Shadowhoof
  accept 5057                         -- Past Endeavors, +50
  turnin 5057

